Exarust

Exarust is an independent, open-source runtime for Exanima, written in Rust
on the Bevy engine. It is licensed under the Apache License, Version 2.0; see
LICENSE.

Exanima, its assets and trademarks belong to Bare Mettle Entertainment Ltd.
(https://www.baremettle.com/).
Exarust is not affiliated with or endorsed by Bare Mettle. Exarust contains
no game assets and no code from the original game; it reads data from an
installation the user already owns.

The project was inspired by IW4L (https://github.com/vladtrc/iw4L), which
does the same for Call of Duty: Modern Warfare 2, and follows its project
layout and working conventions.
